==='''Chapter 3'''===
One of the most brutal Outbreaks in the game, as it combines swarms of some of the most vicious peons thus far (including Metal Doge) and disruptive burrows from Thrillerz and Zuche, all while restricting the player to 15 units deployed at a time.

The 200% Wild Doges mandate the use of [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayers]], especially those with good generalist stats, like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]]. Good [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wavers]] like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] are also vital to keep the peon waves from becoming overwhelming. It's also recommended to send out an occasional [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critter]] to prevent the Metal Doges from going out of hand; however, at least one Metal Hippoe should be kept in order to act as a stepping stone for [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] units like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and especially [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]]. [[Holy Blast]] is recommended to minimize disruption from the Zombies' burrowing.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]: Catasaurus is the Critical Hit user of choice for this stage due to its bulk, low cost, and overall reliability. Be careful not to send out too many of them, lest you kill all of the Metal Hippoes and lose a stepping stone.
*[[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]]: Future Cat's resistance to Metal and Relic makes it a great meatshield for this stage, helping reduce the pushing power of the Metal Doges and Sir Rels.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] / [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]: Both serve to keep the peon count in check with their [[Wave Attack]]s. Jelly Dumpling is preferred for its higher attack power and disposability, but Manic Macho Legs can be used if Jelly Dumpling isn't owned yet.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier is an excellent option against the Wild Doges, and his generalist stats let him deal good damage to the Sir Rels and Ribbos as well.
*[[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]]: While not as strong against the Wild Doges, Cat Chief is still an excellent option for a Behemoth Slayer, and can get rid of the Thrillerz and Zuches for good.
*[[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]]: Has good overall bulk and damage, and proves excellent against the Wild Doges thanks to having both Behemoth Slayer and Strong Vs. Traitless.
*[[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]]: The premier sniper for this stage, as he's able to break the Ribbos' barrier by using the Metal Hippoes as a stepping stone.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: Another solid sniper, Housewife trades Barrier Breaker for better generalist damage (especially if her Savage Blow [[Talents|Talent]] is maxed out) and Zombie Killer.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]]/[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]]/[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]], etc: The True Forms of the Uncanny Legends Mythic Cats are great picks for this stage, as they all have anti-Relic abilities and Curse Immunity alongside Behemoth Slayer.
*Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: With a good line of meatshields, he can be used to clear all non-Metal peons very quickly, buying time for your other critters to kill the Metal Hippoes and Metal Doges.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Detective Vigler (Uber Rare Cat)|Section Chief Gravicci]]: In addition to having an excellent Research Combo with [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Madame Sumo/Riceball Cat]] ([[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|Cheating Heart?]]), Gravicci can handle the Sir Rels and Zombie peons with ease if his Target Relic and Curse Immune Talents are unlocked. His Ultra Form, Arcane Commissioner Gravicci, borderline trivializes this stage thanks to his increased Wave Level and decreased foreswing.
*[[Bliza (Uber Rare Cat)|Blizarena]]: Able to Z-Kill the Thrillerz and Zuches with ease, and can also remove the Ribbos from the census thanks to her Barrier Breaker and immunity to Warp. Do be sure to keep her well protected, however, as the Sir Rels' Curse can cripple her.
*[[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Atlantis Logistix]]: While mostly useful for having an excellent [[Cat Transport (Combo)|Worker Start Level Up combo]] with the vital Courier Cat, they can still contribute thanks to their relatively low cost and ability to obliterate the Thrillerz and Zuches.
*[[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-10 Gigapult]]/Talented [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Saviors]]: Both are great generalist Iron Legions who, in addition to annihilating the Zombies, also match up well into the Sir Rels thanks to their Relic targeting. However, investing into their Ultra Forms solely for this stage is absolutely overkill, especially since the latter requires their Curse Immune talent unlocked in order to reliably take on Sir Rel.

